<%#
  A LINKED FILE'S TWO CONTROLS, written once for its tile (projects/_file_tile) and its list row
  (projects/_file_rows) — the List view lost both until 2026-11-02 (the UX audit's C8), which left
  a Linked file in List with no way to detach it or bring it into the folder. Detach severs the
  reference and keeps the file; Move into project is Maker::AttachToProject#relocate under the
  file's own name, the door the collision prompt's "Move it in as…" posts to.

  RENDERED FOR EVERY ROW AND DRAWS NOTHING FOR ONE THAT IS NOT LINKED, so the decision lives here
  once rather than at both callers. `tile: true` wraps the pair in the tile's `.tile-meta` corner.

  Locals: row (a Maker::ProjectFolderListing::Row), node (its Node), tile (Boolean). Reads @project.
%>
<% if row.linked? %>
  <%= tag.div(class: ("tile-meta" if tile)) do %>
    <%= button_to "Detach", attachment_path(row.attachment), method: :delete, class: "linkbtn danger small tile-detach",
                  form: { data: { turbo_confirm: "Detach #{node.name} from #{@project.name}? The file stays in your library." } } %>
    <%= button_to "Move into project", relocate_project_attachments_path(@project),
                  params: { node_id: row.node_id }, class: "btn small tile-move" %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
